---@class posthog.batch_exports.HogQLQueryModifiers
---@field bounceRateDurationSeconds? number|distilled.Null
---@field bounceRatePageViewMode? posthog.batch_exports.BounceRatePageViewMode|string|distilled.Null
---@field convertToProjectTimezone? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field cookielessTrafficIsRegular? boolean|distilled.Null Do not treat a missing user agent as automation on cookieless events. Positive bot signals and custom project rules still apply. Resolved server-side; not intended to be set by clients.
---@field customBotDefinitions? posthog.batch_exports.HogQLQueryModifiersCustomBotDefinitionsList|distilled.Null
---@field customChannelTypeRules? posthog.batch_exports.HogQLQueryModifiersCustomChannelTypeRulesList|distilled.Null
---@field dataWarehouseEventsModifiers? posthog.batch_exports.HogQLQueryModifiersDataWarehouseEventsModifiersList|distilled.Null
---@field debug? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field forceClickhouseDataSkippingIndexes? posthog.batch_exports.HogQLQueryModifiersForceClickhouseDataSkippingIndexesList|distilled.Null If these are provided, the query will fail if these skip indexes are not used
---@field formatCsvAllowDoubleQuotes? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field inCohortVia? posthog.batch_exports.InCohortVia|string|distilled.Null
---@field inlineCohortCalculation? posthog.batch_exports.InlineCohortCalculation|string|distilled.Null
---@field materializationMode? posthog.batch_exports.MaterializationMode|string|distilled.Null
---@field materializeRepeatedCTEs? boolean|distilled.Null Reuse eligible bounded event aggregates within one query execution. When unset, the server may enable it via the cloud feature flag.
---@field materializedColumnsOptimizationMode? posthog.batch_exports.MaterializedColumnsOptimizationMode|string|distilled.Null
---@field mergeFederatedAggregateJoins? boolean|distilled.Null Merge sibling aggregating LEFT JOINs over federated Postgres tables into one UNION ALL join, so their scans overlap
---@field negatedPersonFiltersNotIn? boolean|distilled.Null Replace negated person-property filters in the WHERE of an `events` query (such as `email not_icontains`) with `person_id NOT IN (SELECT id FROM persons WHERE <the filters fail>)`, so the query no longer joins every person. Applies only when every filtered person property has a materialized column, nothing else in the query reads that persons join, and the join would be a LEFT JOIN.
---@field optimizeJoinedFilters? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field optimizeProjections? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field parserMode? posthog.batch_exports.ParserMode|string|distilled.Null HogQL parser backend; absent → `rust_py_with_cpp_shadow` (rust-py is primary, cpp runs as a sampled shadow). `*_shadow` modes return the primary result and sample-compare against the other parser, reporting divergences without failing the request. The `rust_py_*` modes drive the same hand-rolled Rust parser as `rust_*` but build `posthog.hogql.ast` dataclass instances directly via PyO3, skipping the JSON round-trip.
---@field personIdPushdown? boolean|distilled.Null Push an `id IN (SELECT person_id FROM <left table> WHERE …)` predicate into the joined persons subquery, so the latest-version lookup only reads persons that the outer query's left-table filters can reach. Applies only to a persons join from the query's own FROM table.
---@field personsArgMaxVersion? posthog.batch_exports.PersonsArgMaxVersion|string|distilled.Null
---@field personsJoinMode? posthog.batch_exports.PersonsJoinMode|string|distilled.Null
---@field personsOnEventsMode? posthog.batch_exports.PersonsOnEventsMode|string|distilled.Null
---@field propertyGroupsMode? posthog.batch_exports.PropertyGroupsMode|string|distilled.Null
---@field pushDownPredicates? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field s3TableUseInvalidColumns? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field sessionIdPushdown? boolean|distilled.Null Push a `session_id_v7 IN (SELECT … FROM events WHERE …)` predicate into the raw_sessions subquery to limit aggregation to sessions that participate in the outer events filter.
---@field sessionPropertyPreAggregation? boolean|distilled.Null Pre-filter raw_sessions aggregation by `session_id_v7 IN (cheap pre-aggregation that only materializes the columns referenced by the outer-WHERE session predicate)`. Useful when the breakdown/SELECT pulls in many session columns (e.g. `$channel_type`) but the filter only references one (e.g. `$entry_current_url`).
---@field sessionTableVersion? posthog.batch_exports.SessionTableVersion|string|distilled.Null
---@field sessionTimestampBufferMinutes? number|distilled.Null Padding, in minutes, on each side of the event time range when it filters the sessions table by session start. Defaults to 3 days. It can only narrow the range: values above the default are ignored. Lower it only for a query that keeps just the sessions that start inside its own time range.
---@field sessionsV2JoinMode? posthog.batch_exports.SessionsV2JoinMode|string|distilled.Null
---@field timings? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field typeAwareCastSimplification? boolean|distilled.Null Remove provably redundant casts and nullability wrappers (e.g. `toString(String)`, `assumeNotNull(non_nullable)`, dead `ifNull` fallbacks) using inferred expression types
---@field useMaterializedViews? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field useNewEventsSchema? boolean|distilled.Null Read events from the native JSON events table (`true`) or the legacy events table (`false`). When unset, a staff person's `ph_new_events_schema` cookie applies, then the project's listing in the `CLICKHOUSE_HOGQL_USE_NEW_EVENTS_SCHEMA_TEAMS` instance setting, then the `CLICKHOUSE_HOGQL_USE_NEW_EVENTS_SCHEMA` instance setting. This is an internal rollout switch, and the project settings API ignores it.
---@field usePreaggregatedIntermediateResults? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field usePreaggregatedTableTransforms? boolean|distilled.Null Try to automatically convert HogQL queries to use preaggregated tables at the AST level *
---@field useWebAnalyticsPreAggregatedTables? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field webAnalyticsFirstPageviewFilters? boolean|distilled.Null Serve filters on the stored session-entry attribution properties (`$channel_type`, `$entry_utm_*`, `$entry_referring_domain`) by recomputing the value from the session's first pageview. Resolved server-side; not intended to be set by clients.

