---@class posthog.batch_exports.ListBatchExportsRunsRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field batch_export_id string The `BatchExport` this run belongs to.
---@field after? string Only return runs created at or after this point. Accepts an ISO-8601 datetime or a relative value like `-7d`. Defaults to `-7d`. Ignored when ordering by `data_interval_start`.
---@field before? string Only return runs created at or before this point. Accepts an ISO-8601 datetime or a relative value like `-1d`. Defaults to now. Ignored when ordering by `data_interval_start`.
---@field cursor? string The pagination cursor value.
---@field ["end"]? string Only return runs whose data interval ends at or before this point. Accepts an ISO-8601 datetime or a relative value like `-1d`. Defaults to now. Only applies when ordering by `data_interval_start`.
---@field ordering? string Which field to use when ordering the results.
---@field start? string Only return runs whose data interval starts at or after this point. Accepts an ISO-8601 datetime or a relative value like `-7d`. Defaults to `-7d`. Only applies when ordering by `data_interval_start`.
---@field status? posthog.batch_exports.ListBatchExportsRunsRequestStatusList Only return runs in these statuses. Repeat the parameter to pass more than one status.

