---Credentials and the provider `endpoint_url` live in the linked s3-compatible Integration.
---Mirrors the non-credential fields of `S3CompatibleBatchExportInputs` in
---`products/batch_exports/backend/service.py`.
---@class posthog.batch_exports.S3CompatibleDestinationConfig
---@field bucket_name string Name of the destination bucket.
---@field region string Region the bucket is in (e.g. 'us-east-1').
---@field prefix string Object key prefix applied to every exported file.
---@field compression? posthog.batch_exports.CompressionEnum|string|distilled.Null Optional compression codec applied to exported files. Valid codecs depend on file_format. * `brotli` - brotli * `gzip` - gzip * `lz4` - lz4 * `snappy` - snappy * `zstd` - zstd
---@field file_format? posthog.batch_exports.FileFormatEnum|string File format used for exported objects. * `Parquet` - Parquet * `JSONLines` - JSONLines
---@field max_file_size_mb? number|distilled.Null If set, rolls to a new file once the current file exceeds this size in MB.
---@field legacy_parquet_extension? boolean Whether Parquet files keep the compression codec in their extension, for example '.parquet.zst' rather than '.parquet'. Parquet records its codec inside the file, so new exports leave it out. An export that already wrote Parquet files before this setting existed keeps it, so that pipelines matching on the old names do not break. Has no effect on JSON Lines, which always carries the codec in its extension.
---@field use_virtual_style_addressing? boolean Use virtual-hosted-style addressing rather than path-style.

